using System.Text.RegularExpressions;

namespace DynamicNotch.Services;

/// <summary>
/// The AI's know-how for harder things on Windows: how to install an app, free up space, see what slows the PC,
/// sort a folder, change the wallpaper, read the battery's health… Each one is a short, tested way to do it (PowerShell
/// 5.1, works on any Windows 10/11 in any language), handed to the AI only with a message that needs it, so other
/// messages don't pay for it. Anything that changes or deletes things still asks first (run_powershell's check).
/// </summary>
public static class AiPlaybook
{
    sealed record Play(string Name, Regex When, string How);

    static Regex R(string pattern) => new(pattern, RegexOptions.IgnoreCase | RegexOptions.Compiled);

    static readonly Play[] Plays =
    {
        new("install an app", R(@"\b(install|instal|installe[rz]?)\s+\S+|\bdownload and install\b|\bt[ée]l[ée]charge[rz]? et installe"),
            "Install with winget (built into Windows 10/11): first run_powershell `winget search --name \"NAME\" --accept-source-agreements --disable-interactivity | Select-Object -First 8` and take the exact ID from the ID column (headers may be in another language), preferring the official publisher. Then `Start-Process winget -ArgumentList 'install --id ID -e --silent --accept-package-agreements --accept-source-agreements' -WindowStyle Hidden` (it runs on after this step; big apps take minutes) and say it's installing. To check later: `winget list --id ID -e`. winget missing: give the official download page (research it), never a random download site."),
        new("uninstall or update apps", R(@"\b(uninstall|d[ée]sinstalle[rz]?|remove the app|update (all )?(my )?(apps|programs|everything)|upgrade (all|apps)|mettre [àa] jour (les )?(apps|applications|logiciels))\b"),
            "Uninstall: `winget list --name \"NAME\" --accept-source-agreements --disable-interactivity` for the exact ID, then `winget uninstall --id ID -e --silent` (asks the user first). No winget entry: open ms-settings:appsfeatures. Updates: `winget upgrade --include-unknown --accept-source-agreements --disable-interactivity` lists them; tell the user what's outdated, and on their yes `Start-Process winget -ArgumentList 'upgrade --all --silent --accept-package-agreements --accept-source-agreements' -WindowStyle Hidden`."),
        new("a Windows setting", R(@"\b(settings?|param[eè]tres?|r[ée]glages?)\b|\b(change|set|turn|switch|open|modify|adjust|change[rz]?|mets|active[rz]?|d[ée]sactive[rz]?|enable|disable)\b.{0,30}\b(night ?light|lumi[eè]re nocturne|resolution|r[ée]solution|scaling|default (browser|app)|navigateur par d[ée]faut|taskbar|barre des t[âa]ches|accent colou?r|mouse|souris|keyboard layout|clavier|language|langue|date|time zone|fuseau|power plan|sleep after|hotspot|vpn|proxy|game ?bar|notifications)\b"),
            "Many settings can't be changed by a script, but the exact Settings page opens at once: open \"ms-settings:PAGE\" (open tool, or `Start-Process ms-settings:PAGE`). Pages: display, nightlight, sound, bluetooth, network-wifi, network-mobilehotspot, network-vpn, network-proxy, defaultapps, appsfeatures, startupapps, personalization-background, colors, themes, taskbar, lockscreen, mousetouchpad, typing, regionlanguage, dateandtime, notifications, quietmomentshome (Focus), powersleep, batterysaver, storagesense, windowsupdate, privacy-microphone, privacy-webcam, privacy-location, printers, gaming-gamebar, signinoptions, clipboard, multitasking, about. Open the page, then say in one line what to click there. Things a script can do directly (volume, dark mode, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, brightness): use do_on_pc."),
        new("change the wallpaper", R(@"\b(wallpaper|fond d'[ée]cran|background image|desktop background|change (my )?background)\b"),
            "Set a picture as wallpaper (full path of a .jpg/.png on this PC; find_files first if needed, or create_image then use the saved file): run_powershell `Add-Type -TypeDefinition 'using System.Runtime.InteropServices; public class DnWall { [DllImport(\"user32.dll\", CharSet=CharSet.Unicode)] public static extern int SystemParametersInfo(int a, int b, string c, int d); }'; [DnWall]::SystemParametersInfo(20, 0, 'FULL\\PATH.jpg', 3)` (returns 1 when done). First read the current one to allow undo: `(Get-ItemProperty 'HKCU:\\Control Panel\\Desktop').WallPaper`, and say what it was."),
        new("free up space", R(@"\b(free|lib[eè]re[rz]?|clean|nettoie[rz]?|empty|vide[rz]?)\b.{0,25}\b(space|espace|storage|stockage|disk|disque|drive|pc|computer|ordi|temp|recycle bin|corbeille|bin)\b|\b(disk|disque|drive|storage|stockage|c:)\s+(is\s+)?(full|plein|almost full)|\b(big(gest)?|large|huge|gros)\s+files?\b|\bhow much (free )?(space|storage)\b|\bespace (libre|disque)\b|\btemp files?\b|fichiers temporaires"),
            "Read first, never delete before the user agrees. Free space: `Get-PSDrive -PSProvider FileSystem | ? Used | select Name,@{n='FreeGB';e={[math]::Round($_.Free/1GB,1)}},@{n='UsedGB';e={[math]::Round($_.Used/1GB,1)}}`. Temp size (MB): `[math]::Round(((gci $env:TEMP -Recurse -File -Force -EA 0 | measure Length -Sum).Sum)/1MB)`. Recycle bin: `$s=(New-Object -ComObject Shell.Application).Namespace(10); $n=0;$z=0; foreach($i in $s.Items()){$n++;$z+=$i.Size}; \"$n items, $([math]::Round($z/1MB)) MB\"`. Biggest files: per folder (Downloads, Videos, Desktop, Documents), `gci FOLDER -File -Recurse -EA 0 | sort Length -Desc | select -First 10 FullName,@{n='MB';e={[math]::Round($_.Length/1MB)}}` (the whole drive is too slow). Show a table, suggest what's safe to remove. On the user's yes: temp `Remove-Item \"$env:TEMP\\*\" -Recurse -Force -EA SilentlyContinue` (files in use stay, that's fine), bin `Clear-RecycleBin -Force`, other files: to the recycle bin, never permanently. Then measure again and say how much was freed."),
        new("what slows the PC", R(@"\b(pc|computer|laptop|ordi|windows|it'?s|is|so|too|very|getting|running)\s+(slow|lent|laggy|lagging)\b|\b(slow|lent)\s+(pc|computer|laptop|ordi)\b|\bfreez(e|es|ing)\b|\bfrozen\b|\bfig[ée]\b|not responding|ne r[ée]pond (pas|plus)|\b(cpu|ram|memory|processor)\s+(usage|use|load|utilisation)\b|task manager|gestionnaire des t[âa]ches|\b(force (close|quit)|end task)\b|\bkill\s+(the\s+)?\w+\s*(app|process)?\b|what'?s (using|eating|taking) (my |all |so much )?(cpu|ram|memory)|using (so much|too much|all) (cpu|ram|memory)"),
            "Measure, don't guess. CPU right now (%, any language): `$n=[Environment]::ProcessorCount; $a=@{}; gps | % { try { $a[$_.Id]=$_.TotalProcessorTime.TotalMilliseconds } catch {} }; sleep -m 1000; gps | % { if ($a.ContainsKey($_.Id)) { try { [pscustomobject]@{Name=$_.ProcessName; CPU=[math]::Round(($_.TotalProcessorTime.TotalMilliseconds-$a[$_.Id])/10/$n,1); RAM_MB=[math]::Round($_.WorkingSet64/1MB)} } catch {} } } | sort CPU -Desc | select -First 8`. Memory: `gps | sort WorkingSet64 -Desc | select -First 8 ProcessName,@{n='MB';e={[math]::Round($_.WorkingSet64/1MB)}}` (one app shows as many processes: add them up by name). Frozen apps: `gps | ? { $_.MainWindowHandle -ne 0 -and -not $_.Responding } | select ProcessName,Id`. Answer with a small table and the likely cause. Closing an app: `Stop-Process -Name NAME` only on the user's yes (unsaved work is lost: say so). Also pc_status for the totals."),
        new("sort or tidy a folder", R(@"\b(organi[sz]e|tidy|clean up|sort|range[rz]?|trie[rz]?|classe[rz]?)\b.{0,30}\b(downloads?|t[ée]l[ée]chargements|desktop|bureau|folder|dossier|files|fichiers|photos|documents)\b"),
            "First a preview, nothing moved: `gci 'FOLDER' -File | group { $_.Extension.ToLower() } | sort Count -Desc | select Name,Count`. Propose subfolders (Images: jpg png gif webp heic; Videos: mp4 mkv mov avi; Music: mp3 wav flac m4a; Documents: pdf docx doc txt xlsx pptx csv; Archives: zip rar 7z; Installers: exe msi). On the user's yes, move with a log so it can be undone: `$log=@(); foreach ($f in gci 'FOLDER' -File) { $d = <subfolder for $f.Extension>; if (!$d) { continue }; $to = Join-Path 'FOLDER' $d; ni $to -ItemType Directory -Force | Out-Null; $dest = Join-Path $to $f.Name; if (Test-Path $dest) { continue }; Move-Item -LiteralPath $f.FullName $dest; $log += \"$dest|$($f.FullName)\" }; $log | Set-Content \"$env:APPDATA\\DynamicNotch\\last-tidy.txt\"; $log.Count`. Never overwrite, never touch subfolders' contents. Say how many moved where, and that it can be undone (move each line back)."),
        new("files: zip, convert, rename", R(@"\b(zip|unzip|compress|compresse[rz]?|d[ée]compresse[rz]?)\b|\bextract\b.{0,30}\b(zip|rar|7z|archive)\b|\b(png|jpe?g|webp|heic|images?|pictures?|photos?)\s+(to|en|into)\s+(jpe?g|png|webp|pdf)\b|\bconvert\b.{0,40}\b(to|en|into)\s+(jpe?g|png|webp|pdf|mp3|mp4|gif|ico)\b|\bresize\b.{0,30}\b(images?|pictures?|photos?|png|jpe?g)\b|\b(rename|renomme[rz]?)\b.{0,30}\b(files|fichiers|photos|all|them|these)\b|batch rename"),
            "Zip: `Compress-Archive -Path 'A','B' -DestinationPath 'OUT.zip'` (add -Force only to replace). Unzip: `Expand-Archive 'IN.zip' -DestinationPath 'FOLDER'`. Picture to jpg/png (keeps the original): `Add-Type -AssemblyName System.Drawing; $i=[Drawing.Image]::FromFile('IN'); $i.Save('OUT.jpg',[Drawing.Imaging.ImageFormat]::Jpeg); $i.Dispose()`. Resize: `$s=[Drawing.Image]::FromFile('IN'); $b=New-Object Drawing.Bitmap $s,W,H; $b.Save('OUT'); $b.Dispose(); $s.Dispose()`. Rename several: first show the before → after list, then on yes `Rename-Item -LiteralPath OLD -NewName NEW` each (skip if the new name exists). Video/audio conversion needs ffmpeg: check `Get-Command ffmpeg -EA 0`; missing: offer to install it (winget Gyan.FFmpeg). Always full paths; end with the new file's path."),
        new("network", R(@"\b(ip( address)?|adresse ip|wi-?fi (name|password|mot de passe)|network name|ssid|internet (is )?(slow|down|not working)|no internet|pas d'internet|flush dns|dns|ping|latency|latence|lag|speed ?test|test (my )?(internet|connection) speed|port \d+|which app uses port)\b"),
            "Local IP: `Get-NetIPAddress -AddressFamily IPv4 | ? { $_.InterfaceAlias -notmatch 'Loopback' -and $_.IPAddress -notlike '169.254*' } | select InterfaceAlias,IPAddress`. Network name and whether it has internet: `Get-NetConnectionProfile | select Name,InterfaceAlias,IPv4Connectivity` (netsh wlan needs location access on Windows 11: don't rely on it). Public IP: `Invoke-RestMethod https://api.ipify.org`. Is it the internet or the PC: `Test-Connection 1.1.1.1 -Count 2 -Quiet` and `Resolve-DnsName google.com -EA 0`; DNS fails but ping works: `ipconfig /flushdns`. A saved Wi-Fi password (only the user's own network, on their ask): `netsh wlan show profile name=\"NAME\" key=clear` and show only the line holding the key (its label is in Windows' language). Speed: open https://www.speedtest.net (ping, download, upload) in the browser. Pings must be quick: at most 3 hosts, all at once, short waits: `$hosts='1.1.1.1','8.8.8.8'; $hosts | % { $h=$_; Start-Job { param($x) $r=Test-Connection $x -Count 2 -TimeoutSeconds 1 -EA 0; \"$x \" + $(if ($r) { [math]::Round(($r | measure Latency -Average).Average) } else { 'no answer' }) } -Arg $h } | Wait-Job -Timeout 6 | Receive-Job` (PowerShell 7 has -TimeoutSeconds; on 5.1 use `ping -n 2 -w 800 HOST`). A game's servers usually don't answer pings: say the real in-game ping is shown in the game's own settings (network stats), and give the ping to a nearby big server as the estimate. Port owner: `Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort PORT -EA 0 | % { (gps -Id $_.OwningProcess).ProcessName }`."),
        new("battery health", R(@"\b(battery (health|life|wear|capacity|report)|sant[ée] (de la )?batterie|[ée]tat de la batterie|usure|cycle count)\b"),
            "Health: `powercfg /batteryreport /output \"$env:TEMP\\dn-battery.html\" | Out-Null; $h = gc \"$env:TEMP\\dn-battery.html\" -Raw; $d=[regex]::Match($h,'DESIGN CAPACITY</span></td><td>([\\d,\\. ]+)mWh').Groups[1].Value; $f=[regex]::Match($h,'FULL CHARGE CAPACITY</span></td><td>([\\d,\\. ]+)mWh').Groups[1].Value; \"design $d / full $f\"` (numbers use the PC's separators: strip them before dividing). Health = full ÷ design, as a %: above 80% is good, under 60% worn. The full report can be opened (open the html). No battery (desktop): say so."),
        new("what's in this PC", R(@"\b(specs?|caract[ée]ristiques|which (gpu|cpu|processor|graphics)|what (gpu|cpu|processor|graphics card)|how much ram|combien de ram|windows version|version de windows|pc model|graphics card|carte graphique|how many (monitors|screens)|screen resolution)\b"),
            "`(Get-CimInstance Win32_Processor).Name; Get-CimInstance Win32_VideoController | select Name,DriverVersion; [math]::Round((Get-CimInstance Win32_ComputerSystem).TotalPhysicalMemory/1GB); (Get-CimInstance Win32_ComputerSystem).Model; (Get-CimInstance Win32_OperatingSystem).Caption`. Screens: `Add-Type -AssemblyName System.Windows.Forms; [System.Windows.Forms.Screen]::AllScreens | % { \"$($_.Bounds.Width)x$($_.Bounds.Height) primary=$($_.Primary)\" }`. Ignore virtual display adapters (Parsec, Meta, Spacedesk) when naming the GPU; a laptop often has two GPUs (integrated + dedicated): name both. Answer as a short table."),
        new("startup and background apps", R(@"\b(startup|start-?up)\s+(apps?|programs?|items?)\b|au d[ée]marrage|\b(launch(es)?|opens?|starts?) (at|on|with) (boot|startup|windows)\b|\bopens? when (i|the pc|my pc|windows) (start|boot)s?\b|\bbackground apps?\b|apps? en arri[eè]re-plan"),
            "List: `Get-CimInstance Win32_StartupCommand | select Name,Command,Location` (the same app can show twice, once per user: list it once). To turn one off, open ms-settings:startupapps and say which switch to flip (safer than editing the registry). Say which ones are usually safe to turn off (updaters, launchers) and which to keep (audio, touchpad, antivirus)."),
        new("power: shut down later, restart, sleep", R(@"\b(shut ?down|shutdown|[ée]teins|[ée]teindre|power off|reboot|cancel (the )?shutdown)\b|\bturn off (the |my )?(pc|computer|laptop)\b|\b(restart|red[ée]marre[rz]?)\s+(the |my )?(pc|computer|laptop|ordi|windows)\b|\b(put|send) (the |my )?(pc|computer|laptop) to sleep\b|\bmets? (le pc|l'ordi) en veille\b|\block (the |my )?(pc|computer|screen)\b|\bsleep mode\b"),
            "Only on a clear ask, and say what will happen. Shut down in N minutes: `shutdown /s /t SECONDS` (cancel: `shutdown /a`). Restart: `shutdown /r /t 60` (a minute to save work; cancel with shutdown /a). Sleep: `Add-Type -AssemblyName System.Windows.Forms; [System.Windows.Forms.Application]::SetSuspendState('Suspend', $false, $false)`. Lock: `rundll32.exe user32.dll,LockWorkStation`. Remind the user to save their work."),
        new("a browser, a site, private window", R(@"\b(incognito|private (window|mode|tab)|navigation priv[ée]e|in (chrome|brave|edge|firefox|opera)|with (chrome|brave|edge|firefox|opera)|dans (chrome|brave|edge|firefox)|open (this |the )?(site|website|link|url|page))\b"),
            "A site in a given browser: `Start-Process brave 'https://…'` (chrome, msedge, brave register their name with Windows; firefox: `Start-Process firefox` only if installed, else its full path). Private: chrome/brave `--incognito`, msedge `-inprivate`, firefox `-private-window`, e.g. `Start-Process brave -ArgumentList '--incognito','https://…'`. No browser named: the open tool with the URL (the default browser). Never invent a URL: search first if unsure."),
        new("Windows look and files view", R(@"\b(show|hide|afficher|masquer)\b.{0,25}\b(file extensions?|extensions|hidden files|fichiers cach[ée]s|desktop icons|ic[ôo]nes du bureau)\b"),
            "File extensions: `Set-ItemProperty 'HKCU:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Explorer\\Advanced' HideFileExt 0` (1 hides). Hidden files: same key, `Hidden 1` (2 hides). Open File Explorer windows show the change after F5 or reopening: don't restart explorer. Desktop icons: do_on_pc."),
        new("print", R(@"\b(print|imprime[rz]?)\s+(this|that|it|my|the (file|document|pdf|page)|ce|le|la|les|\S+\.(pdf|docx?|txt|jpe?g|png))\b|\b(printers?|imprimantes?)\b"),
            "Printers: `Get-Printer | select Name,PrinterStatus` and the default: `(Get-CimInstance Win32_Printer | ? Default).Name`. Print a file (on the user's ask): `Start-Process -FilePath 'FULL\\PATH' -Verb Print` (uses the default printer and the file's own app). 'Microsoft Print to PDF' and 'OneNote' aren't real printers: say so if they're the only ones. Settings: ms-settings:printers."),
        new("Windows updates", R(@"\b(windows update|mises? [àa] jour windows|last update|derni[eè]re mise [àa] jour|is (my )?windows up to date)\b"),
            "Last installed: `Get-HotFix | sort InstalledOn -Desc | select -First 5 HotFixID,InstalledOn`. To check or install: open ms-settings:windowsupdate (scripts can't press its button reliably). Apps (not Windows) are updated with winget: see uninstall or update apps."),

        // ───── documents that look finished ─────
        new("make an Excel file", R(@"\b(excel|xlsx|spreadsheets?|feuille de calcul|tableur|classeur)\b|\b(make|create|build|generate|prepare|cr[ée]e|fais|g[ée]n[ée]re|pr[ée]pare)\b.{0,40}\b(budget|invoice|facture|tracker|suivi|planning|inventory|inventaire|timesheet)\b"),
            "write_file a .xlsx, the content in markdown. Optional '# Workbook title'. One '## Sheet name' per sheet, each with ONE markdown table: the header row, then the data rows; keep each column one kind of value. Write values as values: 1250.5, $1,250.50, 1 250,50 €, 12.5%, dates as 2026-03-01: they become real numbers with the right format (money, %, dates). Anything computed is a formula, never a typed result: it starts with = and is written as if the header were row 1 and the data started in row 2, columns A, B, C… in table order (=SUM(B2:B13), =C2*D2, =AVERAGE(E2:E13), =IF(F2>0,\"Paid\",\"Due\"), =B2/B$14); Pixo moves them to where the table really is. End a numeric table with a row 'Total' (sums by formula). On the line after a table, 'chart: column Sales by month' (or bar, line, pie, area) adds a chart (first column = labels, number columns = series). A short note can follow as a plain line. Realistic, complete values (research prices or facts that change); 6-40 rows usually; no placeholders. Then one line: the path and what's inside (sheets, totals)."),
        new("make a Word or PDF document", R(@"\b(make|create|write|draft|generate|prepare|build|turn|cr[ée]e|fais|r[ée]dige|g[ée]n[ée]re|pr[ée]pare)\b.{0,60}\b(word|docx|pdf|document|report|rapport|letter|lettre|cv|resume|r[ée]sum[ée]|essay|memo|proposal|contract|contrat|guide|manual|manuel|brochure|syllabus|itinerary|itin[ée]raire)\b"),
            "write_file a .docx (or .pdf if asked), the content in markdown, structured like a professional's: '# Title', then ONE short line under it (it becomes the subtitle: purpose, date or author), then '## Section' headings ('### ' for sub-sections) in a logical order; short paragraphs (2-4 sentences); '- ' bullets and '1. ' steps for points and procedures ('  - ' to nest); a | table | for anything compared, scheduled or numeric (numbers right-align by themselves, a 'Total' row is bolded); '> ' for the one key takeaway; **bold** for key terms only; [source](https://…) for references; [page break] on its own line before a new part. A letter: no banner title: sender lines, date, recipient, 'Subject: …', the body, the closing and name, as plain lines. A CV: '# Full Name', a line with title · email · phone · city, then ## Profile, ## Experience (### Role — Company, dates, then bullets of results with numbers), ## Education, ## Skills. PDF holds Latin-alphabet languages only: Arabic, Chinese, Russian… go in a .docx. Complete real content; a placeholder only for what the user must fill in (say which)."),
        new("make a presentation", R(@"\b(presentations?|pr[ée]sentations?|powerpoint|pptx|slides?|slide ?decks?|decks?|diapos?|diaporama|pitch)\b"),
            "write_file a .pptx, the content in markdown: '# Deck title', then one line (the subtitle: what it is, for whom, date); then one '## Slide title' per slide. Each slide: 3-6 bullets of at most ~12 words ('  - ' for a sub-point), or a small | table | (up to ~7 rows × 5 columns), or 1-2 short sentences. Titles state the point ('Sales grew 18% in Q1'), not just the topic. **Bold** the key words. A '# Part' heading alone makes a section divider between parts. End with '## Thank you' and one line under it (contact or next step). 8-12 slides for a normal talk. A line 'Notes: …' under a slide is for the speaker and stays off the slide. Then offer to open it."),

        // ───── more things to do ─────
        new("an email draft", R(@"\b(write|draft|compose|prepare|send|reply|answer|[ée]cris|r[ée]dige|envoie|r[ée]ponds)\b.{0,25}\b(an? |the |un |une |le |la )?(e-?mail|mail|courriel)\b|\bmailto\b"),
            "Write the email in the chat first (Subject: line, then the body: greeting, 2-4 short paragraphs, sign-off). To have it ready in the user's mail app (it never sends by itself): run_powershell `Start-Process ('mailto:' + 'to@example.com' + '?subject=' + [uri]::EscapeDataString('SUBJECT') + '&body=' + [uri]::EscapeDataString(\"BODY\"))` (new lines inside BODY as `n in a double-quoted string). Long bodies (over ~1500 characters) may be cut by some mail apps: then also put the text on the clipboard and say so. Webmail open in the browser: Gmail https://mail.google.com/mail/?view=cm&to=TO&su=SUBJECT&body=BODY, Outlook.com https://outlook.live.com/mail/0/deeplink/compose?to=TO&subject=SUBJECT&body=BODY (each part URL-encoded). Never send an email for the user."),
        new("add an event to the calendar", R(@"\b(add|put|create|schedule|book|ajoute|mets|planifie|cr[ée]e)\b.{0,40}\b(calendar|calendrier|agenda|event|[ée]v[ée]nement|meeting|r[ée]union|rendez-vous|appointment|invite|invitation)\b|\.ics\b"),
            "The calendar tool only reads. To add an event: write_file an .ics file (in Documents, e.g. 'Dentist 2026-03-14.ics') and open it: the user's calendar app shows it with a Save / Add button. Content, one per line: BEGIN:VCALENDAR, VERSION:2.0, PRODID:-//Pixo//EN, BEGIN:VEVENT, UID:<random letters>@pixo, DTSTAMP:<now in UTC, e.g. 20260314T090000Z>, DTSTART:20260314T150000, DTEND:20260314T160000 (local times: no Z), SUMMARY:…, LOCATION:…, DESCRIPTION:…, BEGIN:VALARM, TRIGGER:-PT15M, ACTION:DISPLAY, DESCRIPTION:Reminder, END:VALARM, END:VEVENT, END:VCALENDAR. All day: DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260314 and DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260315. Repeats: RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;BYDAY=MO. Check today's date first (pc_status) for 'next Friday'. Also offer a notch reminder (do_on_pc 'remind me …')."),
        new("a QR code", R(@"\bqr\b|\bqr-?codes?\b|\bcode qr\b"),
            "A QR code as a picture: run_powershell `$t=[uri]::EscapeDataString('TEXT OR LINK'); $out=Join-Path ([Environment]::GetFolderPath('MyPictures')) 'QR code.png'; Invoke-WebRequest \"https://api.qrserver.com/v1/create-qr-code/?size=600x600&margin=16&data=$t\" -OutFile $out -UseBasicParsing; $out`, then open it. It's made by a free web service (the text is sent there): fine for links, contact cards and text; for a Wi-Fi QR (WIFI:T:WPA;S:NETWORK;P:PASSWORD;;) say the password goes through that service and ask first; never encode account passwords."),
        new("run something later or every day", R(@"\b(every (day|morning|evening|night|week|weekday|hour|monday|tuesday|wednesday|thursday|friday|saturday|sunday)|chaque (jour|matin|soir|semaine|lundi)|daily|weekly|at (startup|sign-?in|log ?on)|au d[ée]marrage de windows|schedule (a|the|this) (task|script|backup)|t[âa]che planifi[ée]e|automatically (run|open|start|launch|back ?up))\b"),
            "Windows Task Scheduler, for this user (no admin needed): run_powershell `$a = New-ScheduledTaskAction -Execute 'PROGRAM.exe' -Argument 'ARGS'; $t = New-ScheduledTaskTrigger -Daily -At 9am; Register-ScheduledTask -TaskName 'Pixo - NAME' -Action $a -Trigger $t -Description 'Made by Pixo'` (other triggers: -Once -At (Get-Date).AddMinutes(30); -Weekly -DaysOfWeek Monday,Thursday -At 6pm; -AtLogOn). A web page: -Execute 'explorer.exe' -Argument 'https://…'. A PowerShell job: -Execute 'powershell.exe' -Argument '-NoProfile -WindowStyle Hidden -Command \"…\"'. Show: `Get-ScheduledTask -TaskName 'Pixo - *' | select TaskName,State`; remove: `Unregister-ScheduledTask -TaskName 'Pixo - NAME' -Confirm:$false`. Say exactly when it runs and how to remove it. A one-time reminder is simpler: do_on_pc 'remind me …'."),
